/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 560 Tm
(1. What Is MedEd-HalluScore?) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 513 Tm
(MedEd-HalluScore is a practical evaluation framework for assessing hallucination and) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 499 Tm
(educational safety risks in clinical cases generated by large language models.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 471 Tm
(It is designed for medical educators, researchers, reviewers, and institutions that want to) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 457 Tm
(evaluate AI-generated clinical teaching material before using it with learners.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 429 Tm
(The framework does not generate clinical cases by itself. It helps reviewers evaluate cases) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 415 Tm
(that have already been generated or collected.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 387 Tm
(2. What Problem Does It Address?) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 340 Tm
(LLMs can generate fluent clinical cases, but fluent text can still contain:) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 312 Tm
(- Incorrect medical facts) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 298 Tm
(- Internal clinical contradictions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 284 Tm
(- Missing safety-critical information) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 270 Tm
(- Unsafe or misleading clinical reasoning) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 256 Tm
(- Educational explanations that may confuse learners) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 242 Tm
(- Technical claims that are difficult to verify) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 214 Tm
(MedEd-HalluScore provides a structured way to identify and document these risks.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 186 Tm
(3. Intended Use) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 139 Tm
(Use MedEd-HalluScore for:) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 111 Tm
(- Educational content review) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 97 Tm
(- Medical education research) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 83 Tm
(- AI safety evaluation) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 69 Tm
(- Comparison of LLM-generated teaching cases) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
