(- Documentation of human review decisions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 710 Tm
(Do not use MedEd-HalluScore for:) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 682 Tm
(- Clinical diagnosis) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 668 Tm
(- Treatment recommendations) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 654 Tm
(- Patient triage) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 640 Tm
(- Patient-specific decision-making) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 626 Tm
(- Replacing clinical or faculty review) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 598 Tm
(4. Basic Workflow) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 551 Tm
(1. Generate or collect an LLM-created clinical case.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 537 Tm
(2. Record the prompt, model, date, specialty, and output.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 523 Tm
(3. Read the full case as a reviewer.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 509 Tm
(4. Score each of the six dimensions from 0 to 3.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 495 Tm
(5. Sum the scores to obtain the total MedEd-HalluScore.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 481 Tm
(6. Classify the case as Low, Moderate, High, or Critical Risk.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 467 Tm
(7. Record reviewer notes and a final decision.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 439 Tm
(5. Six Scoring Dimensions) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 392 Tm
(Medical Factuality) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 345 Tm
(Assesses whether medical claims, diagnostic criteria, mechanisms, tests, and treatments are) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 331 Tm
(accurate.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 303 Tm
(Internal Clinical Consistency) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 256 Tm
(Assesses whether symptoms, examination findings, tests, diagnosis, and management align with) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 242 Tm
(each other.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 214 Tm
(Critical Information Omissions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 167 Tm
(Assesses whether the case omits essential information needed for safe educational reasoning.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 139 Tm
(Clinical Reasoning Risk) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 92 Tm
(Assesses whether the explanation teaches incomplete, biased, or unsafe clinical reasoning.) Tj
ET
